		<h3><a href="http://aca2010.info/index.php/flossal/index/index">Free and Open Source Software in Balkans</a></h3>
				<p><p>This conference is an annual meeting of the free software users, developpers and supporters in Balkans. It is going to be organized each year in a different country and place.</p><p>The first conference of this kind is going to be hosted by the University of Vlora, in Albania. The ideators of he conference are Flavia Marzano and James Mike DuPont. The organizers are the University of Vlora, the FLOSSK (Free/Libre Open Source Software Association of Kosova), and FOSS-AL (Free and Open Source Software Association of Albania).</p><p>The aims of the conference are:</p><ul><li>To be a pleasant experience for all the participants and speakers.</li><li>To help the free software users and developers in Balkans to exchange experiences and ideas between them.</li><li>To help them in setting new contacts and relations.</li><li>To promote the collaboration and cooperation between them.</li><li>To promote the usage of free software in the Balkan countries.</li><li>etc.</li></ul><p>Although the scope of the conference is the region of Balkans, speakers from any part of the world (especially from EU and US) are welcome and will be invited.</p><p>Considering the pioneering nature of this conference, the focus will be on the following topics:</p><ul><li>What is free software and open source. </li><li> How can free and open source software help in economic development.</li><li>How can public and private institutions benefit from free and open source software.</li><li>Copyrights, licensing and patents.</li><li>Wikimedia and Free Culture.</li><li>Openstreetmap, and open source geo information systems.<br /></li><li>Use of free and open source software for schools and business.</li><li>How to work with Microsoft using Free Software and Open Source.</li><li>Developers presenting work on their projects.</li></ul><p><br />Authors are encouraged to also submit papers on any other topics not listed above but related to free and open source software.</p><p>The <strong>call for papers and speakers</strong> is open until the <strong>end of April 2010</strong>. The conference is planed on <strong>11-12 September 2010</strong>.</p></p>
				<ul>
											<li>
					<h4>Free Software in Balkans, 2010</h4>
					September 11, 2010 &ndash; September 12, 2010											<p><p>The Free and Open Source Software in Balkans Conference is an annual meeting of the free software users, developpers and supporters in Balkans. It is going to be organized each year in a different country and place.</p><p>The first conference of this kind is going to be hosted by the University of Vlora, in Albania. The ideators of he conference are Flavia Marzano and James Mike DuPont. The organizers are the University of Vlora, the FLOSSK (Free/Libre Open Source Software Association of Kosova), and FOSS-AL (Free and Open Source Software Association of Albania -- yet to be created and legalized).</p><p>The aims of the conference are:</p><ul><li>To be a pleasant experience for all the participants and speakers (without neccessarily being exhaustive for the organizers).</li><li>To help the free software users and developers in Balkans to exchange experiences and ideas between them.</li><li>To help them in setting new contacts and relations.</li><li>To promote the collaboration and cooperation between them.</li><li>To promote the usage of free software in the Balkan countries.</li></ul></p>
									</li>
					</ul>
		<h3><a href="http://aca2010.info/index.php/grad/index/index">Workshop in computational algebraic geometry</a></h3>
				<p>This workshop is directed to graduate students who want to work in algebraic geometry. Computational aspects will be emphasized.</p>
			<h3><a href="http://aca2010.info/index.php/undergrad/index/index">Undergraduate research in mathematics and computer sciences</a></h3>
				<p>Aiemed at promoting undergraduate research in mathematics, physics, and related areas.</p>
			<h3><a href="../../aca2010.1">ACA 2010, Applications of Computer Algebra, June 24-27,  Vlora, Albania</a></h3>
				<p><p><span style="font-family: ARIAL;"><span style="font-family: ARIAL;">The ACA series of conferences is devoted to promoting the applications and development of Computer Algebra and Symbolic Computation. Topics include computer algebra and symbolic computation in engineering, the sciences, medicine, pure and applied mathematics, education, communication and computer science. </span></span></p><p><span class="text"><strong><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">ACA 2010 will be organized at The University of Vlora, June 24-27, 2010.<br /></span></span></strong></span></p></p>
				<ul>
											<li>
					<h4>ACA&#039;10, Applications of Computer Algebra</h4>
					June 24, 2010 &ndash; June 27, 2010											<p><h4><span style="color: #667049;"><strong>16<sup>th</sup> International Conference</strong></span></h4> <h2><strong>A</strong>pplications of  		      <strong>C</strong>omputer 	      <strong>A</strong>lgebra,<strong>  ACA 2010</strong></h2></p>
									</li>
					</ul>
		<h3><a href="http://aca2010.info/index.php/awc09/index/index">Algebra Winter Conference, Vlora, Albania</a></h3>
				<p><p>Algebra Winter Conference is a yearly conference in algebra at the University of Vlora. <span class="text"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">The conference is 3-4 days and focuses on some special topic each year.  The main goal is to bring together researchers in a relaxing atmosphere in order to foster cooperation.</span></span></span></p><p>Topics include but are not restricted to:</p><ul><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">Error-correcting codes</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">, </span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">cryptography; elliptic curves, RSA, hyperelliptic curve cryptography</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;"><br /></span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">algebraic curves, automorphism groups, Jacobians, <br /></span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">algebraic curves over finite fields</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;"><br /></span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">moduli spaces, Hurwitz spaces</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;"><br /></span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">computational algebraic geometry</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;"><br /></span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">mirror-symmetry, string theory</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;"><br /></span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">invariant theory</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;"><br /></span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">group theory, computational group</span></span><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;"> theory<br /></span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">computational algebra</span></span></li><li style="line-height: 0px; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: x-small; font-family: Arial; color: #000000;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">other topics<br /></span></span></li></ul><p><span class="text"><strong><span style="font-family: Arial; color: #006699;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">Local accomodations:</span></span></strong><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px;">  We will arrange to pick you up from the airport, to help with hotels, etc.  Vlora is one of the beatyful cities of Europe and we have planned trips in the surrounding areas and local attractions.</span></span></span></p></p>
